[sliver] The round corner meets the 3 mm back chamfer at an apex. The STEP tessellator emits zero-area triangles there (eight triangles totaling 2.3e-15 mm² across the four corners), whose zero normals give the lint undefined strip dimensions. The analytic STEP is valid; these triangles carry no physical strip.
